Summary
This article discusses how to install Vision Synch for Exchange version 4.0 and higher as well as how to run the replacer module to convert all future EWS items into MS Graph versions ahead of Microsoft's retirement of EWS in Exchange Online.
Discussion
Overview
Microsoft is retiring Exchange Web Services (EWS) for Exchange Online effective October 2026. To maintain synchronization between CompuLaw and Exchange Online, update Vision Sync for Exchange to use Microsoft Graph.
This process applies only to firms currently synchronizing CompuLaw Exchange Sync with Office 365 or Exchange Online.
If your firm synchronizes with on-premises Exchange, no action is required. If your firm plans to migrate to Microsoft 365, contact Aderant Support before proceeding.
Important: Complete all steps in the order provided. Changing the sequence can cause future synchronization issues.
Pause the Scheduled Synchronization Cycle
Pause synchronization before making application changes.
Open Windows Task Scheduler on the Vision Sync for Exchange server.
Locate the scheduled task that runs the CompuLaw synchronization cycle, typically launching VisionSynch.exe.
Right-click the task and select Disable.
Create Required Backups
Before proceeding, create the following backups:
A complete copy of the existing Vision Sync for Exchange application folder.
A current backup of the CompuLawSync SQL database.
Note: You can exclude the Logs folder from the application backup to reduce size.
Note: Confirm you are backing up the synchronization database and not the primary CompuLaw Vision database.
Validate Entra ID Application Permissions
Validate the required Microsoft Entra ID application permissions before updating synchronization settings.
Sign in to Microsoft 365 as an administrator.
Open the Microsoft Entra Admin Center.
Go to App registrations > All applications.
Select the existing Exchange Sync application.
Go to API Permissions.
Confirm the following permissions exist:
