Note: Review the client secret expiration date and renew it if necessary before proceeding.
Note: User.Read.All replaces the previously required Directory.Read.All permission for Exchange synchronization.
Important: Do not remove full_access_as_app until the Replacer.exe process completes.
After confirming or adding permissions:
Click Grant Admin Consent.
Confirm consent is successfully granted.
Apply the Exchange Sync Update
Apply the updated synchronization application files.
Run Vision Sync for Exchange Update.exe.
Install the update over the existing Vision Sync for Exchange folder.
After installation completes, the system continues operating with EWS until you update the configuration settings.
Update the Configuration Schema
Open pimsyncsetup.exe.
Perform a synchronization cycle.
Close the application.
Switch Synchronization Mode
Open the synching.config file in the upgraded Vision Sync for Exchange folder.
Locate the following setting:
Change the value to:
Save the file.
This change enables synchronization through Microsoft Graph.
Run Replacer.exe
The Replacer.exe process converts existing EWS calendar items into Microsoft Graph-based items.
By default, the process scans calendar items beginning 30 days in the past and continuing through all future events.
Key Considerations
Items not yet processed by Replacer.exe do not update through normal synchronization after enabling Microsoft Graph mode.
The process can take several days depending on the amount of calendar data.
Allow the process to complete, or nearly complete for future events, before relying on standard synchronization updates.
Run the Replacer Process
Open Replacer.exe from the Vision Sync for Exchange folder.
Monitor progress and confirm all future events convert successfully.
Resume the Scheduled Synchronization Cycle
After the Replacer.exe process starts, resume scheduled synchronization.
Return to Windows Task Scheduler.
Locate the scheduled task that runs the CompuLaw synchronization cycle, typically launching VisionSynch.exe.
Right-click the task and select Enable.
Confirm synchronization operates normally.
